% Thermal conduction of a sinusoidal internal-energy mode in a frozen 2D periodic box.
% Isotropic (Config.sh as is) or field-aligned (test adds MAGNETIC and a B field in the IC).
%
% Units are arbitrary code units: rho0 = 1, BoxSize = 1, u0 = 1, k = 2 pi.
% ConductionCoeff = kappa = 1/(4 pi^2) gives D k^2 = (kappa/rho0) k^2 = 1, so the theta=0 / isotropic
% mode decays by e over TimeMax = 1. MaxSizeTimestep caps the step at TimeMax/1024 (all cells on one
% bin), ~0.2 of GIZMO's own explicit limit 0.5 dx^2 rho/kappa = 4.8e-3 at 64^2.
%
% The test overrides InitCondFile and OutputDir per case.
InitCondFile                       conduction_step_iso_ics
OutputDir                          output
TimeBegin                          0
TimeMax                            1
BoxSize                            1
TimeOfFirstSnapshot                0
TimeBetSnapshot                    0.125
MaxSizeTimestep                    0.001
MinSizeTimestep                    1e-7
ConductionCoeff                    0.025330295910584444
MinGasTemp                         0
DesNumNgb                          20
MaxNumNgbDeviation                 0.1
CourantFac                         0.4
ErrTolIntAccuracy                  0.01
MaxRMSDisplacementFac              0.1
ErrTolForceAcc                     0.001
ErrTolTheta                        0.7
DivBcleaningParabolicSigma         0.2
DivBcleaningHyperbolicSigma        1.0
TimeBetStatistics                  0.5
MaxMemSize                         1000
ResubmitOn                         0
ResubmitCommand                    none
